WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.701
-What's up, Jimmy?
-Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.634
I have a lot things
to discuss with you.

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:06.167
-Sure.
First is you were

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:11.167
fantastic on the Grammy's, the
50th, the tribute to hip-hop.

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:14.501
50 years -- 50 years of hip-hop.
-Yes, sir.

00:00:14.501 --> 00:00:16.400
-And you crushed it,
everyone did.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.467
What was it like?
What'd it feel like?

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:20.701
-It was good, I mean,
based off the fact that,

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:22.767
you know, the rap category
wasn't televised

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:24.400
on the Grammys
for so many years.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.634
It was -- it was cool.

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:27.100
You know, it's kind of like
full circle for me

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.868
'cause I had actually
won a Grammy

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:31.067
in pre-telecast so I wasn't
able to make

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:32.934
the big speech in front of the
crowd and stuff like that.

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:34.400
-They never aired it?
-Never did.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.901
So, to be on that stage
performing,

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:38.467
oh, man, that was best.
-Yeah.

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:39.868
And what was backstage like?

00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:42.167
-Backstage was crazy because,
you know, that green room,

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:43.467
off the chain.
-Right?

00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:44.501
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:46.767
-I mean Ice-T was in there,

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:48.601
and Ice-T tells
all the best stories.

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:50.300
-Dude, Ice-T is the best.
-He got all the best stories.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.501
-He comes on, I go,
"Just tell me something."

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:53.734
-Facts. I love that dude.

00:00:53.734 --> 00:00:56.300
-Wait, he just said
something about you.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.868
-He said that this is his first
time meeting Wu-Tang Clan.

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:01.734
I doubt if I was there because I
don't remember it,

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:06.033
but he said first time he met us
we were gonna kick his ass.

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:08.968
Or he thought -- he thought we
were gonna kick is ass.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:11.467
But it turns he that, you know,
we were fans, he was a fan,

00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:14.000
and it was all love from there.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.834
-But -- but why would you ever
fight Ice-T?

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:18.200
-We wouldn't, but you know,
back then,

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.434
those where our grimey years.

00:01:19.434 --> 00:01:21.133
Everything we did looked
intimidating.

00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:22.300
You know what I'm saying?
-Yeah, I know

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:24.467
what you're saying.
-Yeah.

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:26.534
-I know, obviously,
you're in Wu-Tang,

00:01:26.534 --> 00:01:29.200
but I heard that your kids first
words were Wu-Tang.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.968
-Yup, my first son.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:32.834
Oh, y'all laughing.
I mean...

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:34.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:36.067
Honestly.
-Isn't that rad?

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:38.267
-I mean, I'm glad
they found it funny

00:01:38.267 --> 00:01:39.767
'cause I'm just glad it
wasn't a curse word.

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:41.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.834
-That's actually good, yeah.
-Yeah, 'cause kids

00:01:42.834 --> 00:01:44.734
pick up on things really quick.
-But his first...?

00:01:44.734 --> 00:01:46.400
-Wu-Tang, mm-hmm.
-Really?

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.000
-Wu-Tang, Wu-Tang, yes, sir.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.601
-We actually found audio
of this.

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:50.701
-This is Method Man's...
-That's dope.

00:01:50.701 --> 00:01:52.634
...son saying his first words,
Wu-Tang.

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:53.634
Listen.

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:54.734
-What's that, Shaquan?

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:56.133
-Wu-Tang.

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:58.133
-What's that?

00:01:58.133 --> 00:01:59.200
-Wu-Tang.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.868 --> 00:02:02.601
-Wu-Tang.
-He's gonna love that.

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:04.634
-Wu-Tang.
-Yeah, he's gonna love that.

00:02:04.634 --> 00:02:07.167
-Did you -- did you just always
have tapes around

00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:08.901
or bring him to the studio?

00:02:08.901 --> 00:02:11.067
-Actually, what I did in that
whole process,

00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:12.534
because he was already
saying it.

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:14.701
What I did was I had this tattoo
of Wu-Tang on my hand

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:15.734
right here, so I would point
to it.

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:17.601
I was like, "What's that
Shaquan? Wu-Tang.

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:20.067
Who's your favorite group,
Shaquan? Wu-Tang."

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:21.701
-So, whatever you do,
he just say that.

00:02:21.701 --> 00:02:23.234
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:23.234 --> 00:02:26.434
-You've been getting
more into acting now recently.

00:02:26.434 --> 00:02:27.701
Congratulations on that.
-Thank you.

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:29.033
-You're crushing it, by the way.

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:33.367
You're really --
I want to get into this.

00:02:33.367 --> 00:02:36.601
Now that the show is going well,
this is Season 3,

00:02:36.601 --> 00:02:39.334
it's getting picked up again,
I want to talk about auditions.

00:02:39.334 --> 00:02:40.868
And do you every remember
any auditions

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:42.367
that didn't go so well?

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:43.767
-Yeah, I'm glad you
brought that up.

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:45.767
-Yeah, no problem. That's why --
that's why I'm here, bud.

00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:48.767
-Alright, so I had to audition
for a movie

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:50.067
called "Money Monster."

00:02:50.067 --> 00:02:51.667
-Okay.
-Jodie Foster directed it,

00:02:51.667 --> 00:02:53.734
George Clooney, I believe,
was staring in it.

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:54.834
And yeah, I had to read.

00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:57.067
So I'm super prepared, right?

00:02:57.067 --> 00:03:01.100
I'm sitting in the waiting room
for, you know, for the read.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.868
Couple of producers show up,
then one more producer shows

00:03:03.868 --> 00:03:04.968
and he's like, "Meth,
you're my guy.

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:06.033
I can't wait till you
go up in there.

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:07.567
Kill it, Meth.
No, no worries.

00:03:07.567 --> 00:03:09.300
No, no worries whatsoever.
Just kill it."

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:12.300
I'm like this is my guy here.
I'm gonna kill it for this guy.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.801
-Yes.

00:03:13.801 --> 00:03:15.667
-But what I didn't know was
there were waiting

00:03:15.667 --> 00:03:16.968
for one more person.

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:18.767
-Okay.
-And that last person showed

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:21.234
up about two minutes later
and it was Jodie Foster.

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.667
Now, for me -- yeah, ooh.

00:03:22.667 --> 00:03:25.667
For me, it was like the same
reaction, oh, man,

00:03:25.667 --> 00:03:27.133
now it's Jodie Foster
in the room

00:03:27.133 --> 00:03:28.467
and I'm a big fan.

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:29.767
Her work speaks for itself.

00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:30.934
-She's the best.

00:03:30.934 --> 00:03:33.267
-I get up in this room, Jimmy,
oh, my God.

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:34.567
Um, alright.

00:03:34.567 --> 00:03:36.167
It started off good, 'cause,
you know,

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:38.334
then I caught a brain fart.

00:03:38.334 --> 00:03:41.300
From there,
I couldn't remember a thing.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.100
So, it gets worse though.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.801
I start sweating. I have a
little mini anxiety attack.

00:03:45.801 --> 00:03:48.434
Start sweating crazy,
so now I'm looking for anything

00:03:48.434 --> 00:03:51.334
in the room to dry myself
off with.

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:53.901
The guy has a box of Kleenex.
-Yeah.

00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:55.100
-If you know anything
about Kleenex,

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.033
when they get wet, what happens?

00:03:57.033 --> 00:03:59.567
So I'm trying to dry myself off
with the Kleenex.

00:03:59.567 --> 00:04:01.133
I got paper stuck to my face.

00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:03.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.400
All I can think
is Jodie Foster thinks

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.334
I'm, like, this idiot right now.

00:04:07.334 --> 00:04:08.601
-[ Laughs ] Exactly.

00:04:08.601 --> 00:04:12.033
-And I kindly excused myself and
walked out, that was it.

00:04:12.033 --> 00:04:13.767
-Did you ever see any
of them ever again?

00:04:13.767 --> 00:04:16.167
-I haven't seen anybody that was
in that room ever again,

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:19.300
but if I ever run it -- if I
ever run into Jodie,

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:22.000
hopefully she doesn't remember

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.300
and I would love
to work with her.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.634
-Yeah, exactly.
-There you go.

00:04:25.634 --> 00:04:27.501
-Well, I love you take that
and you get back up.

00:04:27.501 --> 00:04:29.000
-Yes, sir.
-And you're crushing it on

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.167
"Power Book II."
-Yeah.

00:04:31.167 --> 00:04:32.167
-I want to say congratulations.

00:04:32.167 --> 00:04:33.968
You won two?
-Three.

00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:35.334
-Three Image awards?
-Yeah.

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:36.901
-Come on, bud.

00:04:36.901 --> 00:04:40.000
-And, yeah, the thing about
that, the most important part

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.133
about that is I think
the word Image.

00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:43.400
-Yeah.
-You know what I mean?

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:44.701
-Exactly.
-Especially from the background

00:04:44.701 --> 00:04:46.734
that I come from,
that lets people know

00:04:46.734 --> 00:04:50.467
that you can't count the down
and out out for too long

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:52.501
'cause some day they're
gonna have their day.

00:04:52.501 --> 00:04:55.601
And boy, when it comes, whoo,
it's a beautiful thing.

00:04:55.601 --> 00:04:57.868
-It's a beautiful thing.
-It's a beautiful thing.

00:04:57.868 --> 00:04:59.534
-I hope -- I hope you're
enjoying it.

00:04:59.534 --> 00:05:01.601
-Yes, I am.
-You're crushing it.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:03.868
-Now, on Season Three,
does it get a bit easier

00:05:03.868 --> 00:05:05.234
now that it's kind
of home to you?

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:07.300
You're the people that people
get nervous around you.

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.467
-Yeah.

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:11.267
-People get tissues, tissues
stuck their head

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:12.734
auditioning for you, bud.

00:05:12.734 --> 00:05:14.501
You're the new Jodie Foster,
bud.

00:05:14.501 --> 00:05:15.834
-I would love -- you know what?
I would love

00:05:15.834 --> 00:05:17.634
to be a fly on the wall in some
of these auditions,

00:05:17.634 --> 00:05:19.501
especially for people that's
coming onto this show

00:05:19.501 --> 00:05:20.868
because it's such a big hit now.

00:05:20.868 --> 00:05:22.968
We had great numbers.
-I just saw that.

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:24.767
Yeah, our premiere episode had
great numbers.

00:05:24.767 --> 00:05:26.100
-It already got --
-Thanks to the viewers.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.167
-It already got picked up
for another season.

00:05:27.167 --> 00:05:28.534
-Yeah, for another season.

00:05:28.534 --> 00:05:31.033
We're actually filming
Season four now,

00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:32.834
and I'm way over my quota
in nude scenes

00:05:32.834 --> 00:05:34.267
so you might want
to check it out.

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:35.267
-[ Laughs ] My God.

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:36.567
-For real.

00:05:36.567 --> 00:05:38.868
-How do we explain
"Power Book II: Ghost"

00:05:38.868 --> 00:05:40.000
and who you play?

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.767
-I play a lawyer named
Davis Maclean.

00:05:41.767 --> 00:05:44.434
"Power" is a spin-off of the
original "Power" series

00:05:44.434 --> 00:05:47.400
which was done brilliantly
by Omari Hardwick,

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:50.767
Courtney Kemp
and 50 Cents project.

00:05:50.767 --> 00:05:53.267
So this is the spin-off,
and it's based of off

00:05:53.267 --> 00:05:56.400
the original character's son,
played by Michael Rainey.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.334
Basically, him trying to
navigate through life

00:05:58.334 --> 00:06:00.300
